  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "Two routes, one saved definition", "items": [
      "Preview runs in this browser and requires the tab to stay open. The command clones the chosen version before execution.",
      "Durable runs use the server library's exact version. The queued definition survives closing the tab; an enabled worker processes it.",
      "Both runners inject the shared executor registry into workflow-core. Browser normalization preserves legacy canvas defaults."
    ] },
    { "dot": "amber", "title": "Inputs, computation and saving differ", "items": [
      "HTTP source rows and captured document evidence are replayed from saved configuration. Running does not refresh those sources.",
      "Missing HTTP input fails unless example data was explicitly enabled; malformed document captures fail. Block findings remain in the result.",
      "A preview result is recorded locally before asynchronous library sync. A failed save stays dirty; a revision conflict blocks later writes."
    ] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "Access, failures and recovery", "items": [
      "Durable POST, cancel and retry require a current session and Owner/Editor membership. Viewers can read; local preview is a separate path.",
      "A missing server version or unavailable tool rejects admission. Wait for a successful library save before starting a newly saved version durably.",
      "Worker throws retry within the attempt limit; block errors are recorded. A cancellation flag suppresses the completed result; it is not mid-block interruption.",
      "The UI can retry a failed/cancelled run using its original definition. Evidence describes committed code at 444d6e0, not a live execution test."
    ] }
